description:
North star: compile work proportional to input. A fact derived from source alone (a function's static reach) must be computed once for the whole compile, not once per root, and must not depend on which roots exist.

Fact (spike B, 2026-10-09, scratch reach/B, patch reach/B/spike.patch on 4a412b66a): pull.rs addresses every product inside a per-RootId session (ProductKey lives in a root's ProductSessions). A product derived only from facts, such as ProductKey::Reach over StaticCallees, has no root. Borrowing one is unsound both ways tried:
- the first submitted root: every program fails with "compiler2 root 0 product path waited on an executable's runtime demand with no ready producer" (the borrowed session drags in that root's backend preconditions);
- the last submitted root: fixtures/00593_quote_unquote_lambda_occurrences_distinct miscompiles ("function main/0 is not defined"), because macro expansion mints roots mid-compile (quoted_expander.rs, world.macro_root); recursive_callable_input_sources_settle_in_either_root_order fails with the same no-ready-producer error.

Goal: the product layer has an address space for products whose inputs are facts only, shared by every root and every job, with the same read, validation, invalidation and recursive-group settlement (pending_strong_component) as rooted products. A job can read such a product and wait on it when it is pending on a missing fact.

Paper first: the key space, who owns the session, how a job's read is recorded and woken, how invalidation reaches readers in every root.

Acceptance:
- spike B's Reach(Static) product, ported onto it, passes fixtures/00593 (run, interp, build) and recursive_callable_input_sources_settle_in_either_root_order;
- census outputs identical against the base commit; no pin rises;
- no root is borrowed anywhere.
